  "about": "I believe that one-in-a-million edge cases happen every day at scale, and I build systems to handle them.\n\nMy path to software engineering started in clinical medicine. As a med student, I learned to work with complex systems where precision is everything. Today, as an engineer at Amazon, I apply that same rigorous problem-solving to distributed cloud architecture.\n\nI am an engineer who loves to look under the hood. I don't just want to know that an application runs; I want to understand how the software actually hits the metal. My work centers on high-concurrency Rust, low-latency data platforms, and massive-scale Kubernetes infrastructure. Whether I am building zero-copy cache servers in Rust or architecting resilient Java microservices, I thrive in high-traffic environments.\n\nI also believe that great technology comes from teamwork. Working together and sharing ideas always builds stronger systems than anyone could build alone. Most importantly, I am a fun person to talk to, and I am more than a few lines of description! Feel free to reach out and get to know me :)",
